{
  "id": "hedra",
  "name": "Meris Hedra",
  "transport": "meris",
  "folder": "Meris Hedra",
  "noDim": true,
  "source": "Meris Hedra manual (global settings pp. 2-4, presets §8, MIDI CC table §9), https://www.analoguehaven.com/meris/hedra/manual.pdf; MIDI in via a Chase Bliss MIDIbox (port jumpered for Meris), verified on ch 15 2026-10-24",
  "liveNote": "the Hedra can't be asked anything — live controls, preset select, and a library of presets kept in edit (saving on the pedal is Alt)",
  "setup": [
    "MIDI comes in on the EXP jack through a MIDI-to-TRS box (Meris MIDI I/O, or a Chase Bliss MIDIbox output jumpered for Meris) with a stereo TRS cable. In only — the box sends nothing back.",
    "On the pedal: hold Alt (left LED switch) while powering up; LEDs blink 3 times. Pitch 3 to max = EXP jack is MIDI. Pitch 2 = channel (binary on the LEDs; max = omni). Power-cycle to save.",
    "Give it its own channel — CCs shared with the OBNE pedals mean different things there (CC 14 = Hedra bypass, Dark Star mix, Black Fountain dry).",
    "edit keeps your presets (Dropbox): store files the sound under the preset number; selecting that number later recalls the pedal's preset and pushes edit's copy on top. To keep it in the pedal too, hold Alt on the pedal after.",
    "MIDI notes tune the pitch voices: one held note sets Pitch 1, two set 1 + 2, three set all three; note off mutes that voice."
  ],
  "groups": [
    {
      "id": "pitch",
      "name": "Pitch"
    },
    {
      "id": "alt",
      "name": "Alt"
    },
    {
      "id": "delay",
      "name": "Delay"
    },
    {
      "id": "switches",
      "name": "Switches"
